# init Call-Flow Code-Reading Notes

Start at `pkg/apis/kubeone/v1beta2/zz_generated.conversion.go`. This file centralizes type conversions in the v1beta2 package. When tracing the call flow, first pause at two early declarations: `init` on line 34 and `RegisterConversions` on line 40.

```go
func init() {
func RegisterConversions(s *runtime.Scheme) error {
```

`init` is the entry point for package initialization, and `RegisterConversions` receives `*runtime.Scheme`. Taken together, these two points establish that this section handles conversion registration, not defaulting for a particular resource.

The later part of the file starts showing bidirectional functions for specific types:

```go
func autoConvert_v1beta2_APIEndpoint_To_kubeone_APIEndpoint(
func Convert_v1beta2_APIEndpoint_To_kubeone_APIEndpoint(
func autoConvert_kubeone_APIEndpoint_To_v1beta2_APIEndpoint(
func Convert_kubeone_APIEndpoint_To_v1beta2_APIEndpoint(
```

Lines 664 and 672 are a pair of reference points from v1beta2 `APIEndpoint` to `kubeone.APIEndpoint`; lines 676 and 684 are the reverse pair. Further down, line 688 has already entered `AWSSpec`, so it should not be mixed into the same section of notes as the APIEndpoint conversion.

To fill in: verify what is actually submitted to the scheme in the body of the `init` function, as well as the handoff points between each public `Convert` function and its corresponding `autoConvert` function.
